From f2b5fed364c7b5782a7abd2e9e0e92149c6c3e7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fi3 <you@example.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 01:25:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ADD selected-agent slash command routing to keep provider
 commands off prompt sends

Selected-agent chat input that begins with a non-whitespace slash is provider control input, not ordinary prompt content. The backend contract exposes a command operation with a streaming variant, and Codex implements it as raw resume stdin so commands such as /status and /fork reach the provider without prompt wrapping.
