@@ -166,6 +172,10 @@ The primary public methods are:
 
 `CommandChat` uses the active `AgentProfile` when launching user agents, reviewers, and linearizers.
 Workflow code must not hard-code `AgentKind::Codex` when the active profile supplies the provider.
+When UI-driven selected-agent chat input starts with `/` followed by a non-whitespace character,
+`CommandChat` treats that input as a provider command and routes it through `AgentBackend::run_command`
+or `run_command_streaming` instead of the normal prompt send path. This keeps provider commands such
+as Codex `/status` and `/fork` distinct from ordinary user prompt text.
 
